  lastSentAt : timestamptz
  --
  send_outstanding_arrangement_reminders() «pg_cron hourly»
}

User "1" -- "0..1" AccountRole : has >
User "*" -- "1" Role : roleId >
AccountRole ..> AccountRoleName
Event ..> EventStatus
Notification ..> NotificationKind

User "1" -- "*" Event : organiser <
Event "*" -- "0..1" User : coordinator >
(Event, User) .. CoordinatorAssignment

Event "1" *-- "*" EventAuditLog
EventAuditLog "*" -- "0..1" User : actor >
Event "1" *-- "*" Clarification
Clarification "*" -- "1" User : sender >
Notification "*" -- "1" User : recipient >
Notification "*" -- "0..1" Event : about >
NotificationReminderSettings "0..1" -- "1" User : coordinator's cadence >
NotificationReminderReceipt "*" -- "1" Event
NotificationReminderReceipt "*" -- "1" User : recipient >
AccountRole ..> ActingRole : request acts as one held role

note right of CoordinatorAssignment
  Event Coordinator Lead only (event_request.assign_coordinator).
  PATCH /api/event-requests/:eventId/coordinator: assigns or
  reassigns; unassigned -> submitted; history row
  field_name 'coordinator_id'; notices kind coordinator_assigned.
  Queue: GET /api/assignment-queue (SG2-87/97).
end note

note bottom of ActingRole
  SG2-104: an account may hold several roles; each request
  acts as exactly one, named in X-Acting-Role (default: the
  least-privileged role held). The database repeats the choice
  in acting_role(), so RLS never grants more than the account holds.
end note

note bottom of Notification
  In-app only. Hold notices (venue_hold_notifications) are a
  separate table, merged into the same inbox (SG2-69). Cancelled
  events and registrations are announced by event_cancelled /
  registration_* kinds (SG2-60/61/62/63/67).
end note

legend bottom left
  |= Marker |= Meaning |
  |<back:#FFFFFF>   plain   </back>| built before Week 7, or by a later backlog story (story id where given) |
  |<back:#FFF4CC> <<Week 7>> / «W7» </back>| Week 7 change (story id) |
  Multiplicity [0..1] = nullable column. SG2-xx without a marker colour = later backlog story.
endlegend
@enduml

