note bottom of VenueOperations
  Setup before + turnaround after widen every
  availability / conflict check (SG2-78);
  existing pairs that now clash are flagged
  as BookingClash (SG2-79).
end note

note bottom of VenueBookingDisruption
  SG2-81: new flag notifies Coordinator; Preparation/Confirmed
  returns to Planning, clears confirmation and notifies Organiser.
  Approval of a replacement atomically releases its old booking
  and cancels its old request (202610170001). Other event details stay.
  Pending replacement requests reserve nothing.
end note

note bottom of ChangeOneVenue
  SG2-83 (202610210002): only the event's assigned coordinator
  cancels a booking (venue_bookings.release); other bookings of
  the event are cancelled only when named in the same call. Each
  cancellation keeps who, when and why on the booking and in the
  event history; Venue Staff get venue_booking_cancelled /
  venue_change_requested notices. On a Confirmed or Preparation
  event the event returns to Planning with a venue recheck.
end note

note bottom of Venue
  SG2-106: delete_venue() refuses while the venue has a current or
  future booking, a live hold on a current or future period
  or a pending request, and otherwise
  keeps the row (deletedAt) so history still shows its name.
end note

