@startuml class-safety-changes
!pragma layout smetana
title ConnectSphere domain model (4/5): safety check, change requests & cancellation\nas of main 4881413 (3 Nov 2026)
hide empty members
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BackgroundColor<<Week 7>> #FFF4CC
  BackgroundColor<<ref>> #E8F0FE
}

class Event <<ref>> {
  eventId : int
  status : EventStatus
  outstandingArrangements : jsonb
  safetyCheckRevision : bigint
}
class User <<ref>> {
  userId : uuid
}
class VenueBookingRequest <<ref>> {
  requestId : bigint
}
class EquipmentRequest <<ref>> {
  requestId : bigint
}

class SafetyCheck <<Week 7>> {
  .. no table: events in awaiting_safety_check, SG2-91 ..
  safety_check_queue()
  refresh_safety_check_status() «trigger path»
  event_safety_approved()
  safety_approval_gate «trigger, SG2-94»
}

class SafetyDecision <<Week 7>> {
  decisionId : bigint
  decision : approve|reject|request_changes
  {field} reason : string [0..1] (<= 2000)
  {field} arrangements : venue|equipment|other (array)
  decidedBy : uuid
  decidedAt : timestamptz
  --
  record_safety_decision() «SG2-92»
  rework_safety_rejected_event() «SG2-92 AC4»
}

class SafetyRereview <<Week 7>> {
  reviewId : bigint
  arrangement : venue|equipment
  flaggedAt : timestamptz
  resolution : confirmed|withdrawn [0..1]
  resolvedBy / resolvedAt [0..1]
  --
  safety_rereview_queue()
  confirm_safety_rereview() «SG2-93»
}

class EventChangeRequest {
  changeRequestId : bigint
  field : proposed_date|expected_attendance|venue_requirements|
    accessibility_needs|equipment_requirements|name|purpose|description
  fromValue : jsonb [0..1]
  toValue : jsonb
  {field} reason : string (<= 1000)
  status : pending|accepted|refused
  createdAt : timestamptz
  decidedBy / decidedAt [0..1]  «SG2-65»
  {field} decisionReason : string [0..1]  (required when refused)
  --
  raise_event_change_request() «SG2-64»
  apply_accepted_event_change() «SG2-66»
  decide_event_change_request() «SG2-65»
  settle_arrangement_recheck() «SG2-66»
}

class EventCancellation {
  .. no table: events.cancellation_* and cancelled_* columns, SG2-67 ..
  request_event_cancellation()
  cancel_event()
  keep_cancelled_events_cancelled() «trigger»
}

SafetyCheck "*" .. "1" Event : checks (awaiting_safety_check) >
SafetyCheck ..> SafetyDecision : decided by
SafetyDecision "*" -- "1" Event : about >
SafetyDecision "*" -- "1" User : decided by Safety Officer >
SafetyRereview "*" -- "1" SafetyDecision : sent back by >
SafetyRereview "*" -- "1" Event
SafetyRereview "*" -- "0..1" VenueBookingRequest : venue (Venue Staff)
SafetyRereview "*" -- "0..1" EquipmentRequest : equipment (Technical Support)
SafetyRereview "*" -- "0..1" User : resolved by >

EventChangeRequest "*" -- "1" Event : about >
EventChangeRequest "*" -- "1" User : requested by organiser >
EventChangeRequest "*" -- "0..1" User : decided by coordinator >
(Event, User) .. EventCancellation

note bottom of SafetyDecision
  Append-only (select + insert only). The latest decision, when
  Approve and the event is still in Preparation or Confirmed, is
  the event's safety approval. Approve -> preparation; Reject ->
  safety_rejected (coordinator rework -> planning, safety_other_recheck
  outstanding); Request Changes -> planning, named arrangements marked
  safety_venue_recheck / safety_equipment_recheck / safety_other_recheck.
  A decision on a stale safetyCheckRevision is refused (202610190006).
end note

note bottom of SafetyCheck
  Hand-off (SG2-91): an Approved or Planning event with every venue
  request approved and every required equipment reserved moves to
  awaiting_safety_check; it moves back to Planning when one falls
  through. Preparation is reachable only through an Approve decision
  (SG2-94); confirm_event() lists 'safety' as outstanding otherwise.
end note

note bottom of EventChangeRequest
  Service-role only; the API shows a request to the owning organiser
  and the assigned coordinator. Accepting a significant change on a
  Preparation or Confirmed event returns it to Planning and marks
  venue_recheck / equipment_recheck / registration_recheck outstanding.
end note

note bottom of EventCancellation
  The creating organiser asks with a reason; only the assigned coordinator
  cancels. cancel_event() releases not-yet-ended bookings and tentative holds,
  cancels pending venue and equipment requests; the SG2-56 trigger releases
  equipment reservations. Registered attendees and the organiser get
  event_cancelled. A cancelled event never changes status again.
end note

legend bottom left
  |= Marker |= Meaning |
  |<back:#FFFFFF>   plain   </back>| built by a later backlog story (SG2-64/65/66/67) |
  |<back:#FFF4CC> <<Week 7>> / «W7» </back>| Week 7 change #6, operational safety check (SG2-91/92/93/94) |
  |<back:#E8F0FE> <<ref>> </back>| defined on another page |
  Multiplicity [0..1] = nullable column.
endlegend
@enduml

